    "finding": "Threshold arithmetic reproduces calibration-only selection. However every held-out positive literal was already in the approval registry; guarded recall is not unseen-wording generalization. A membership-to-family lookup could reproduce the guarded admission outcomes without embeddings. Only three canonical source vectors were stored, so the raw cosine scores are genuine query-to-source retrieval, not cached query vectors.",
    "limits": "Recomputation cannot prove the absence of human inspection or pretrained-data overlap. The approval registry is not an independent semantic correctness oracle. Metadata-only component cases need explicit wire context; bare text alone stays eligible."
